{"step_index":143,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-02T11:13:20Z","thinking":"There are exactly 16 conversation summaries. A check is needed to determine if the active conversation directory resides within a specific location. The question is whether data replication can safely read an active directory. This is assessed by examining the characteristics of the tool. It's safe to use because certain file types are excluded, ensuring no locking occurs.\n\n\nA structure for the session synchronization process needs definition, including file placement and directory organization.  This ensures discoverability and maintainability. A testing framework will validate the synchronization. Documentation updates are necessary to explain its usage.\n\n\nThe process begins by validating the user executing the session sync, ensuring it isn't the root user unless specifically configured. Next, the home directory of the user and the root of the project repository are determined. Finally, directories for source and destination are set.\n\n\nNow, the script defines the source and destination paths for AI session data. Subdirectories will be ensured to exist for different session types, while creating a symbolic link for easier access, conditionally. A .gitignore file is deployed within the sessions directory to prevent sensitive files from being tracked.\n\n\nA README file is being deployed to the session directory, providing users with information about the session archive's purpose and structure. The script will also check for the existence of different session source directories to ensure they're available for synchronization.\n\n\nAntigravity CLI brain sessions are being synchronized using a file synchronization tool.  History data is copied directly.  A session index file needs generation from a database. This index facilitates session retrieval.\n\n\nA session index file needs to be generated by querying the session summary database.  The summaries are extracted, formatted as JSON, and written to a file for later lookup. Individual project sessions from another AI tool will be synchronized using a file synchronization tool, which will ensure that the target directory reflects the source, including deletions if requested. History data is copied separately. Another AI CLI tool's sessions will be synchronized using the same file synchronization method.\n\n\nSession data from the AI CLI tool, \"Codex,\" will be synchronized. The script checks if the source session directory exists. If it does, the tool will synchronize the \"sessions\" subdirectory. A copy operation will handle `session_index.jsonl` and `history.jsonl` if those files are present in the source.\n\nActive git branch detection and resolution will occur to facilitate future operations. Uncommitted changes within the session directory will be identified using a version control system. Based on the presence of uncommitted changes, staged changes are added using a version control staging command.\n\n\nA version control system will be used to commit and push the synchronized session data. The commit will occur only if changes exist and both commit and push actions are enabled.  A status report will summarize the synchronization, including whether each session type was synchronized, and if version control operations occurred successfully.\n\n\nThe synchronization process needs to account for the initial run scenario where the playbook itself might be new or modified in the repository, thus requiring its commit to ensure the playbook's availability within the version control system.  Standard Ansible syntax should define if the commit action was successfully executed. A potential symbolic link setup should be investigated.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"---\n# Playbook pour synchroniser les sessions des 3 assistants IA en ligne de commande :\n# - Antigravity CLI (agy) : ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/\n# - Claude Code : ~/.claude/projects/\n# - Codex CLI : ~/.codex/sessions/\n#\n# Copie les sessions vers le répertoire `sessions/` (sous-dossiers agy/, claude/, codex/)\n# du dépôt LINUX, puis effectue un git add, git commit et git push vers GitHub.\n#\n# Utilisation manuelle :\n#   ansible-playbook sync-ai-sessions.yml\n#   ansible-playbook playbooks/sync-ai-sessions.yml\n#\n# Options utiles :\n#   -e git_push=false       (synchronise et commite localement sans pousser)\n#   -e git_commit=false     (synchronise uniquement sur le disque)\n#   -e sync_delete=true     (supprime les sessions distantes si effacées localement)\n#   -e max_file_size=30m    (taille maximale par fichier, 50m par défaut pour respecter GitHub)\n#\n- name: Synchronize AI CLI sessions (Antigravity, Claude Code, Codex) and push to GitHub\n  hosts: localhost\n  connection: local\n  gather_facts: true\n  vars:\n    ai_sessions_user: \"{{ lookup('env', 'SUDO_USER') or lookup('env', 'USER') }}\"\n    sessions_dir_name: \"sessions\"\n    git_remote: \"origin\"\n    git_branch: \"\"  # Détecté automatiquement sur la branche active si vide\n    git_commit: true\n    git_push: true\n    sync_delete: false\n    max_file_size: \"50m\"\n    rsync_extra_args: >-\n      --exclude='*.sock'\n      --exclude='*.socket'\n      --exclude='*.lock'\n      --exclude='*.pid'\n      --exclude='*.db-shm'\n      --exclude='*.db-wal'\n      --exclude='*.db-journal'\n      --exclude='*.key'\n      --exclude='*.pem'\n      --exclude='*credential*'\n      --exclude='auth.json'\n      --exclude='.remember/tmp'\n      --exclude='.remember/capture-alive.d'\n      --max-size={{ max_file_size }}\n\n  tasks:\n    - name: Valider l'utilisateur exécutant\n      ansible.builtin.assert:\n        that:\n          - ai_sessions_user | length > 0\n          - ai_sessions_user != 'root' or (ansible_facts.user_id == 'root' and ai_sessions_user | length > 0)\n        fail_msg: \"Impossible d'identifier l'utilisateur propriétaire des sessions IA.\"\n\n    - name: Trouver le dossier personnel de l'utilisateur\n      ansible.builtin.getent:\n        database: passwd\n        key: \"{{ ai_sessions_user }}\"\n\n    - name: Découvrir la racine du dépôt git\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: git -C \"{{ playbook_dir }}\" rev-parse --show-toplevel\n      register: _repo_root_cmd\n      changed_when: false\n\n    - name: Définir les variables de chemin\n      ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n        user_home: \"{{ ansible_facts.getent_passwd[ai_sessions_user][4] }}\"\n        repo_root: \"{{ _repo_root_cmd.stdout.strip() }}\"\n\n    - name: Définir les chemins sources et destinations des sessions\n      ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n        sessions_base_dir: \"{{ repo_root }}/{{ sessions_dir_name }}\"\n        agy_src: \"{{ user_home }}/.gemini/antigravity-cli\"\n        agy_dest: \"{{ repo_root }}/{{ sessions_dir_name }}/agy\"\n        claude_src: \"{{ user_home }}/.claude\"\n        claude_dest: \"{{ repo_root }}/{{ sessions_dir_name }}/claude\"\n        codex_src: \"{{ user_home }}/.codex\"\n        codex_dest: \"{{ repo_root }}/{{ sessions_dir_name }}/codex\"\n\n    - name: Créer l'arborescence cible pour les sessions\n      ansible.builtin.file:\n        path: \"{{ item }}\"\n        state: directory\n        mode: '0755'\n      loop:\n        - \"{{ sessions_base_dir }}\"\n        - \"{{ agy_dest }}\"\n        - \"{{ claude_dest }}\"\n        - \"{{ codex_dest }}\"\n\n    - name: Créer le lien symbolique ai-sessions -> sessions\n      ansible.builtin.file:\n        src: \"{{ sessions_dir_name }}\"\n        dest: \"{{ repo_root }}/ai-sessions\"\n        state: link\n        force: true\n      when: sessions_dir_name != \"ai-sessions\"\n\n    - name: Déployer le fichier .gitignore protecteur dans sessions/\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        dest: \"{{ sessions_base_dir }}/.gitignore\"\n        mode: '0644'\n        content: |\n          # Sockets, verrous et PIDs d'exécution\n          *.sock\n          *.socket\n          *.lock\n          *.pid\n\n          # Fichiers temporaires SQLite WAL / SHM\n          *.db-shm\n          *.db-wal\n          *.db-journal\n\n          # Clés privées, certificats, secrets et jetons d'authentification\n          *.key\n          *.pem\n          *credential*\n          *secret*\n          auth.json\n          .env\n\n          # Fichiers transitoires et caches\n          .remember/tmp/\n          .remember/capture-alive.d/\n          __pycache__/\n          *.pyc\n          .DS_Store\n\n    - name: Déployer le fichier README.md de documentation dans sessions/\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        dest: \"{{ sessions_base_dir }}/README.md\"\n        mode: '0644'\n        content: |\n          # AI CLI Sessions Archive\n\n          Ce dossier archive de manière structurée l'ensemble des sessions de travail issues des assistants d'ingénierie IA en ligne de commande :\n\n          - **`agy/`** : Sessions d'Antigravity CLI issues de `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/`. Contient les journaux complets de conversation (`transcript.jsonl`), scratchpads, artefacts produits, ainsi qu'un index des conversations (`session_index.jsonl`).\n          - **`claude/`** : Sessions de Claude Code issues de `~/.claude/projects/`, organisées par projet (`-home-koby`, etc.) avec les transcriptions JSONL et artefacts associés.\n          - **`codex/`** : Sessions de Codex CLI issues de `~/.codex/sessions/`, ordonnées chronologiquement (`YYYY/MM/DD/`), avec le fichier d'index `session_index.jsonl`.\n\n          ### Mise à jour manuelle\n\n          Pour synchroniser les sessions locales et pousser les modifications sur GitHub :\n\n          ```bash\n          cd ~/LINUX\n          ansible-playbook sync-ai-sessions.yml\n          ```\n\n    - name: Vérifier la présence des répertoires et fichiers sources\n      ansible.builtin.stat:\n        path: \"{{ item.path }}\"\n      loop:\n        - { key: 'agy_brain', path: \"{{ agy_src }}/brain\" }\n        - { key: 'agy_history', path: \"{{ agy_src }}/history.jsonl\" }\n        - { key: 'agy_summaries', path: \"{{ agy_src }}/conversation_summaries.db\" }\n        - { key: 'claude_projects', path: \"{{ claude_src }}/projects\" }\n        - { key: 'claude_history', path: \"{{ claude_src }}/history.jsonl\" }\n        - { key: 'codex_sessions', path: \"{{ codex_src }}/sessions\" }\n        - { key: 'codex_index', path: \"{{ codex_src }}/session_index.jsonl\" }\n        - { key: 'codex_history', path: \"{{ codex_src }}/history.jsonl\" }\n      register: _src_stats\n\n    - name: Convertir les vérifications sources en dictionnaire\n      ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n        src_exists: \"{{ _src_stats.results | items2dict(key_name='item.key', value_name='stat.exists') }}\"\n\n    # =========================================================================\n    # 1. Antigravity CLI (agy)\n    # =========================================================================\n    - name: Synchroniser les sessions Antigravity CLI (brain)\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: >-\n          rsync -av\n          {{ '--dry-run' if ansible_check_mode else '' }}\n          {{ '--delete' if sync_delete else '' }}\n          {{ rsync_extra_args }}\n          \"{{ agy_src }}/brain/\" \"{{ agy_dest }}/\"\n      register: _sync_agy\n      changed_when: \"'Number of created files: 0' not in _sync_agy.stdout and (_sync_agy.stdout_lines | length > 4)\"\n      when: src_exists.agy_brain\n\n    - name: Copier l'historique prompt d'Antigravity CLI (history.jsonl)\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        src: \"{{ agy_src }}/history.jsonl\"\n        dest: \"{{ agy_dest }}/history.jsonl\"\n        mode: '0644'\n      when: src_exists.agy_history\n\n    - name: Générer l'index des sessions Antigravity CLI (session_index.jsonl)\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: >-\n          python3 -c \"\n          import sqlite3, json, sys\n          src, dst = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\n          conn = sqlite3.connect(src)\n          rows = conn.execute('SELECT conversation_id, title, last_modified_time FROM conversation_summaries ORDER BY last_modified_time DESC').fetchall()\n          with open(dst, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n              for r in rows:\n                  f.write(json.dumps({'id': r[0], 'thread_name': r[1], 'updated_at': str(r[2])}) + '\\n')\n          \" \"{{ agy_src }}/conversation_summaries.db\" \"{{ agy_dest }}/session_index.jsonl\"\n      when: src_exists.agy_summaries and not ansible_check_mode\n      changed_when: false\n\n    # =========================================================================\n    # 2. Claude Code\n    # =========================================================================\n    - name: Synchroniser les sessions Claude Code (projects)\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: >-\n          rsync -av\n          {{ '--dry-run' if ansible_check_mode else '' }}\n          {{ '--delete' if sync_delete else '' }}\n          {{ rsync_extra_args }}\n          \"{{ claude_src }}/projects/\" \"{{ claude_dest }}/\"\n      register: _sync_claude\n      changed_when: \"'Number of created files: 0' not in _sync_claude.stdout and (_sync_claude.stdout_lines | length > 4)\"\n      when: src_exists.claude_projects\n\n    - name: Copier l'historique prompt de Claude Code (history.jsonl)\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        src: \"{{ claude_src }}/history.jsonl\"\n        dest: \"{{ claude_dest }}/history.jsonl\"\n        mode: '0644'\n      when: src_exists.claude_history\n\n    # =========================================================================\n    # 3. Codex CLI\n    # =========================================================================\n    - name: Synchroniser les sessions Codex CLI (sessions)\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: >-\n          rsync -av\n          {{ '--dry-run' if ansible_check_mode else '' }}\n          {{ '--delete' if sync_delete else '' }}\n          {{ rsync_extra_args }}\n          \"{{ codex_src }}/sessions/\" \"{{ codex_dest }}/\"\n      register: _sync_codex\n      changed_when: \"'Number of created files: 0' not in _sync_codex.stdout and (_sync_codex.stdout_lines | length > 4)\"\n      when: src_exists.codex_sessions\n\n    - name: Copier l'index des sessions de Codex CLI (session_index.jsonl)\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        src: \"{{ codex_src }}/session_index.jsonl\"\n        dest: \"{{ codex_dest }}/session_index.jsonl\"\n        mode: '0644'\n      when: src_exists.codex_index\n\n    - name: Copier l'historique prompt de Codex CLI (history.jsonl)\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        src: \"{{ codex_src }}/history.jsonl\"\n        dest: \"{{ codex_dest }}/history.jsonl\"\n        mode: '0644'\n      when: src_exists.codex_history\n\n    # =========================================================================\n    # 4. Git Commit & Push\n    # =========================================================================\n    - name: Détecter la branche active git\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: git -C \"{{ repo_root }}\" rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD\n      register: _git_branch_cmd\n      changed_when: false\n\n    - name: Déterminer la branche git cible\n      ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n        resolved_git_branch: \"{{ git_branch if (git_branch | length > 0) else _git_branch_cmd.stdout.strip() }}\"\n\n    - name: Vérifier les modifications non commitées dans sessions/\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: git -C \"{{ repo_root }}\" status --porcelain \"{{ sessions_dir_name }}\" ai-sessions\n      register: _git_status\n      changed_when: false\n\n    - name: Indexer (git add) les sessions\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: git -C \"{{ repo_root }}\" add \"{{ sessions_dir_name }}\" ai-sessions\n      when:\n        - not ansible_check_mode\n        - git_commit\n        - _git_status.stdout | length > 0\n\n    - name: Créer le commit git pour les sessions\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: >-\n          git -C \"{{ repo_root }}\" commit -m\n          \"chore(sessions): sync AI CLI sessions [agy, claude, codex] ({{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }})\"\n      when:\n        - not ansible_check_mode\n        - git_commit\n        - _git_status.stdout | length > 0\n      register: _git_commit_res\n\n    - name: Pousser (git push) les sessions vers GitHub\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: git -C \"{{ repo_root }}\" push \"{{ git_remote }}\" \"{{ resolved_git_branch }}\"\n      when:\n        - not ansible_check_mode\n        - git_push\n        - git_commit\n        - _git_status.stdout | length > 0\n      register: _git_push_res\n\n    - name: Rapport récapitulatif\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg:\n          - \"Dossier sessions : {{ sessions_base_dir }}\"\n          - \"Sessions Antigravity (agy) : {{ 'OK' if src_exists.agy_brain else 'IGNORÉ (source absente)' }}\"\n          - \"Sessions Claude Code : {{ 'OK' if src_exists.claude_projects else 'IGNORÉ (source absente)' }}\"\n          - \"Sessions Codex CLI : {{ 'OK' if src_exists.codex_sessions else 'IGNORÉ (source absente)' }}\"\n          - \"Modifications git détectées : {{ (_git_status.stdout | length > 0) }}\"\n          - \"Commit git effectué : {{ _git_commit_res is defined and not _git_commit_res.skipped | default(false) }}\"\n          - \"Push GitHub effectué : {{ _git_push_res is defined and not _git_push_res.skipped | default(false) }}\"\n          - \"Statut : {{ 'Sessions poussées vers ' ~ git_remote ~ '/' ~ resolved_git_branch if (_git_status.stdout | length > 0 and git_push) else 'Les sessions sont déjà synchronisées. Aucun push requis.' }}\"\n","Description":"Création du playbook sync-ai-sessions.yml pour synchroniser et pousser les sessions agy, claude et codex vers GitHub","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/sync-ai-sessions.yml","toolAction":"Writing sync-ai-sessions playbook","toolSummary":"Write sync-ai-sessions.yml"}}]}
